{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1148938-technocratic-awakening","id":1148938,"title":"Technocratic Awakening","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-11T17:19:25-07:00","id":1148938,"title":"Technocratic Awakening","content":"Hi there.<br /> <br /> I can imagine this has been asked in this forum thousands of times, but anyway. Is the technocratic awakening different from a regular one? I cant find any description in Guide To The Technocracy or Mage 20 (thanks in advance if you can tell me the specific pages).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T17:49:13-07:00","id":1148945,"title":"","content":"Yep! It depends on the individual Technocrat and is heavily influenced by their convention and paradigm, of course, but their Enlightenment should be different than a mystic's Awakening. Not mechanically, but in story.<br /> <br /> Example Tradition Awakening: a woman goes to an EDM show, dances wildly, maybe pops a few mystery pills, and time starts to flow differently around her. Some people are thrashing at a faster-than-possible speed while another guy is headbanging in slow motion. The woman realizes that her perception of time has been altered, but then has the idea to try and look into the future. She has experienced a mystical awakening that most Cultists of Ecstasy would identify with.<br /> <br /> Example Technocratic Awakening: a woman is working late for an investment firm and wants to bump her clients' portfolio above $1,000 this quarter. While keeping an eye on their portfolio's stock prices and occasionally trading a few, she also tries out micro-financing by investing in farmers in the developing world. She knows her clients have put their trust, their BELIEF in her, knows that for several of them they need her to make a profit to get their kids through school. She takes that belief and channels it through the investments. The knowledge that she is not just moving around numbers, but moving around BELIEF surges through her like electricity. The next week her portfolio's value increases to over $1,400, higher than she had hoped for her clients. The farmers she had invested in have used the money to buy seed, growing yams in West Africa to ship around the world. She doesn't know exactly how she's aware of this, but she KNOWS that this was more than just a long night of work getting to her. She knows because she did it again and increased the portfolio's value to $2,600.<br /> <br /> (Did I mention I like the $yndicate?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10653-omegaz","name":"OmegaZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10653_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T19:35:31-07:00","id":1148968,"title":"","content":"This is GOLD. Thank you very, VERY much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T21:43:54-07:00","id":1148992,"title":"","content":"Sometimes it's flavored by the character's eventual Technocratic allegiance - especially if the character Awakened while already a member of the Union. But first and foremost, a mage's Awakening is idiosyncratic and personal. Anything can induce a worldview-shattering revelation, from a near-death experience, to seeing something of transcendent beauty, to a <i>really good</i> sexual encounter, to something as seemingly small as learning something that makes it all &quot;click&quot;.<br /> <br /> While the Awakening's nature could color the mage's understanding of the world, biasing what magical or technomagical style they pursue, sometimes they are fundamentally lost...until one mage organization or another happens upon them and makes a good pitch.<br /> <br /> One Technocrat might have seemed Fated to join a mystic Tradition, until the Union found them. So the mage ended up being trained as a scientist...but still has dreams of flying through space on a horse made of glass, catching the stars in his hand and carrying a flaming sword. Not all Technocrats are entirely comfortable in their lot; most, for obvious reasons, tend to stay quiet about fanciful dreams or superstitionist flights of fancy. And if they occasionally have visions of some god or legendary figure, they'll either shake it off, or try to see it as a metaphor their subconscious mind is using to convey some more orderly message.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T22:28:22-07:00","id":1148998,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not sure. While some people may seem custom made for a Tradition or Convention, for the most part both sides desperately fight to gain the same recruits, regardless of their background. The Awakening should probably transcend the mystical/Science based dichotomy, though their may be superficial resemblances to one group or another. At its heart, Awakening is a sudden realization about the self and its place in the universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T07:01:24-07:00","id":1149081,"title":"","content":"As I recall, barring immediate induction into the Technocracy...<br /> <br /> Imagine you're a scientist or an engineer. Working on something revolutionary and it works, something clicks and the world becomes clearer, you start spitting out theories to justify your experiments... But the experiments always seem to fail in the light of day.<br /> <br /> Then, when it looks like your career is in ruins.. someone takes you aside and explains what happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}